meta {
  name: eligible-batches
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseURL}}/inventory/drugs/{{drugId}}/batches
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  availability: usable
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Get Eligible Drug Batches

  Returns positive-quantity physical batches for one drug in the authenticated workspace. This endpoint supports operator guidance and explicit damaged/expired disposal; it does not choose batches for patient or ward dispensing.

  ## Authorization

  Requires an authenticated user with an active workspace membership.

  ## Path Parameters

  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  |-----------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `drugId` | UUID | Yes | Drug Master record in the authenticated workspace. |

  ## Query Parameters

  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  |-----------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `availability` | string | Yes | `usable` returns batches expiring today or later. `expired` returns batches whose expiry date is before today. Boundaries use the workspace timezone. |

  ## Ordering

  Results use deterministic FEFO order: `expiryDate`, then `createdAt`, then batch `id`.

  ## Success Response

  **`200 OK`**

  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Drug batches fetched successfully",
    "data": {
      "batches": [
        {
          "id": "batch-uuid",
          "batchNumber": "BATCH-001",
          "expiryDate": "2027-12-31",
          "quantityAvailable": 40
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Notes

  - No cost, workspace, actor, or internal audit fields are exposed.
  - An unknown drug or a drug with no eligible batches returns an empty array.
  - Patient and ward stock-out requests must not submit a batch ID; the backend applies FEFO automatically.

  ## Errors

  | Status | Description |
  |--------|-------------|
  | `401 Unauthorized` | Authentication is invalid or workspace access is suspended. |
  | `422 Unprocessable Entity` | The path UUID or availability value is invalid. |
}
